   102	
   103	Every crew that had lain up for the cold was there, and a good many carters. The hide-woman had a stool by the hearth, and the three grey men had their board on a keg and were not throwing. It was the hour at which a one-armed man read out what the day had brought to his plank; and the room had gone quiet for it, as it had on a night of first snow, when a crew came in with white on its shoulders.
