editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/whole-arc-read.md:79:The two pages remain unjoined. The closest approach deliberately occupies opposite ends of Brom's blanket and is stopped before inference (`chapter-52.md:153–195`). No dialogue, narration or cutaway connects the leaf to lamps, sigils, Arbiters, plates or stations as a finding. Vastin's sentence stops in the chamber, at the blanket and again in his own court-night interior (`chapter-38.md:219–239`; `chapter-52.md:177–195`; `chapter-59.md:325`).
