editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-B-REPORT.md:194:All thirty chapters were inside the three ranges before (13.3–14.2; 2.5–4.5%; 850–1,050) and all thirty are inside them after. No sentences were joined. The narrow places that shaped where I could cut: ch37 (853 words a scene: 24 words of room; I took 7), ch40 (859), ch35 (mean 13.40), ch43 and ch46 (≥40 share 2.6%), ch42, ch50 and ch57 (mean 14.11–14.16, where cutting a short sentence lifts the mean), ch53 (≥40 share 4.4%).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/state/completion/LANE-B-REPORT.md:215:- ch36 "It was a hand wide, and he found that he was glad to know it." I had cut "he found that"; `sweep_probe` then showed ch36 close 11% -> 12%. I found which of the chapter's four changes did it by reverting them one at a time on scratch copies (the source was not opened), restored the line, and the figure returned to 11%.
