+# Book 8 listening proof — part 3 reading notes
+
+Scope: `manuscript/chapter-31.md` through `chapter-45.md`. Each chapter was printed whole with line numbers and read in full, in order. The boundary snippets below are the first and last six whitespace-delimited words of every scene, copied from the manuscript; markdown marks remain where they fall in those words. No manuscript file was modified, and no git command was run.
+
+## Chapter 31 — One at a Time — 5 scenes
+
+1. `Karis sat up that night against` … `since a store behind a chimney.` — Karis's private method and the figure/word reasoning remain clear aloud; no unattributed speech.
+2. `The book came down from the` … `and went back to his page.` — Lane join at line 71 is ruled sound in the dedicated join section below. Cleon's rough-voice questions, Karis's answers and the unnamed lamp-boy remain distinct.
+3. `"Read the rest, then," said Lira,` … `and he bent to his page.` — The ten-letter work and Cleon's closing `Good` are attributable; the number sequence is coherent.
+4. `Seln was at the ladder's foot` … `"No," said Lira. "Nor did you."` — Six-person loft council is audible: Seln gives the surveillance finding, Brom supplies the card inference, Vastin answers his earlier failure, Cael rules, and Lira closes privately.
+5. `Brom paid at the half-door in` … `will be wanted in the morning.` — Purse moves to a hundred and thirty-four; Lira's ladder practice and Cael's anticipatory lamp movement are clear. Clean.
+
+## Chapter 32 — No Round — 5 scenes
+
+1. `The fourteenth letter came out of` … `at the foot, the gate shut.` — The party's stair order and the gate closure are spatially clear; the old man is Vastin throughout.
+2. `It did not swing to, as` … `that place there is no round.` — Fight setup is clear by position: two below, four above, Vastin facing uphill, one crossbow, one dark lantern.
+3. `It was Brom who met the` … `on the other end of it.` — Brom, Lira and Karis each retain a separate action line; `the flat` is the courier's flat, not flat ground.
+4. `Cael had turned back uphill before` … `the eleventh time, in that stair.` — Every refusal is explicit. The eleventh's first voice, *This far?*, follows the still wall rather than a deployment and cannot be mistaken for spoken dialogue.
+5. `The hand came away from the` … `one, and it's the wrong one."` — Seln's cord intervention, the six attackers' withdrawal and Cael's count of eighty-one are clear. Long paragraph at line 189 is listed in the proof.
+
+## Chapter 33 — Entered — 5 scenes
+
+1. `They let the old man down` … `to explain that card to anybody."` — Injury roll is clear: Lira right shoulder, Brom both shoulders, Karis left palm, Vastin knee. Seln's mild voice enters from above without ambiguity.
+2. `There was a house inside the` … `glad that it was the left."` — Treatment scene is audible: the registered healer is rejected because the name would be entered; Brom sews seven stitches; Lira holds the light.
+3. `Vastin could not hold a bowl.` … `close its hand upon a bowl.` — The eleventh acquisition unit is intact and wholly italic. `Eleven.` gives the narrator a clean landing after the notice.
+4. `"I should be obliged for a` … `can't hold a cup," said Lira.` — Vastin's three-headed account stays one formal voice. The protected `I put the wall…` / `It's entered` exchange is attributable, and the debt discussion distinguishes permission to tell from permission to take.
+5. `Seln came down off the ladder's` … `which way it would be wanted.` — Seln's finding, the log, initials `V.` and `S.`, deployment thirty-two and the protected eleventh entry all flatten intelligibly in document voice.
+
+## Chapter 34 — The Carts' Street — 5 scenes
+
+1. `They let the old man down` … `what it costs when I do."` — Yard council and card arithmetic are clear. Seln's repeated rules are recognizably quoted back, not a new speaker.
+2. `A handcart went up a hill` … `rattled out onto the carts' street.` — Gate counts `one, and four` remain coherent; Vastin's role as matter on Karis's card is audible.
+3. `It was a road that a` … `be spared the trouble of deciding."` — Beam-man is the only unnamed speaker. `Whose?` is answered by Karis; Vastin's restrained sentence does not blur into hers.
+4. `The clerk had the green book` … `without a word, for the ash.` — Clerk, dusty-coated keeper and Vastin are separated by location and tags; the twenty-seven-step descent is clear.
+5. `The eleventh had nothing to do` … `two things laid foot to foot.` — Cleon's quoted `What's that? / Which lays? / Hm` is framed as recalled speech. No broken join after the lane's restored `old man` wording at line 177.
+
+## Chapter 35 — Lean — 6 scenes
+
