editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md:291:Cael held the case by its foot, and Vastin had the strap's end shut in his fist. At every tread the two raw hands went to the stone, and the sound leg thrust, and the whole length of him was hitched one step higher into the dark, backward, with the case drawn after him like a thing being brought up out of a well. They were face to face, and Cael could not see the face. He could hear it breathe, a yard above his own, and he bore up the weight of a cord and a mallet and one stake, so that it should not pull upon that hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/manuscript/chapter-35.md:297:*Rune-adjacent. Cleon. Partial. Rune family. A made thing's lean — the direction a maker put in it; which mark bears, which is borne, which is nothing; whether a run sits or goes. Structure, not meaning: it will tell me a thing is an instruction and will not tell me what it instructs. Made things only. Not a river. Not a man. Costs the eyes, after. No use in a fight. Engagement field: inscriptive — the second field that is not a fight, after clinical; given, not taken. Tier equivalent unknown. Deployment: none. Twelfth.*
